{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And what is the reason for mentioning 'and he begot in his likeness, after his image'? That HaShem placed in him the power of generation to bring forth his likeness, so that his deed resembles that of the Most High. And he did not say thus concerning Cain and Abel, nor did he mention how many years Cain lived, nor how many years he was when he begot his son Enoch, because the name of Abel and also Cain was blotted out in the Flood. And the killing of Cain is mentioned to show the righteousness of HaShem — and if He prolonged His anger, He punished him in the end, as in the sense of 'and will by no means clear' (Exodus 34:7)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:22.067103326Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}